am.jsonl:{\"event\":\"result\",\"result\":{\"conversation_id\":\"63b740db-b42b-4982-a7f8-cc9005961731\",\"status\":\"SUCCESS\",\"response\":\"### D2 — Routes Come From the Record: Completed\\n\\n#### 1. Summary of Changes\\n- **Dynamic Route Derivation from Site \\u0026 Release:**\\n  - In [`src/api/methods/routes.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/src/api/methods/routes.ts), [`routeTable()`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/src/api/methods/routes.ts#L46-L108) accepts `requires?: readonly string[]` (from `release.requires`). Routes are filtered so only contracts required by the active release are exposed. Unused grants in `site.mesh.contracts` are omitted.\\n  - In [`src/api/api.service.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/src/api/api.service.ts), [`ApiService.handle()`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/src/api/api.service.ts#L174-L248) resolves incoming Host to `Site` via [`cdn.resolve_site`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/src/cdn/tools/resolve_site.ts#L21-L56), looks up the active `Release` if `site.releaseHash` is set, and constructs the route table filtered by `release.requires`.\\n  - In [`src/api/tools/describe.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/src/api/tools/describe.ts), replaced `site.find_one` with [`cdn.resolve_site`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/src/cdn/tools/resolve_site.ts#L21-L56) and passed `release?.requires` to [`routeTable()`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/src/api/methods/routes.ts#L46-L108).\\n- **Matching CDN Cache \\u0026 Invalidation:**\\n  - In [`src/api/api.service.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/src/api/api.service.ts), `tableFor()` caches route tables keyed by `${site.id}:${releaseHash}:${site.updatedAt?.toISOString() ?? ''}`.\\n  - `siteFor()` caches hostname lookups in memory, with negative caching (`null`) for unknown hostnames to eliminate repeated database round-trips for 404s.\\n  - Subscribes to both `cdn.site_deployed` and `site.updated` broker events to invalidate the host cache (`this.sites.delete(host)`).\\n- **Zero Cast Compliance:**\\n  - Removed all `as ReturnType\\u003c...\\u003e` casts. Zero `as any`, zero `as never`, zero casts across the implementation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### 2. Reusing `cdn.resolve_site` vs. Adding a Door\\n- **Decision:** Reused [`cdn.resolve_site`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/src/cdn/tools/resolve_site.ts#L21-L56). Zero new doors or bypasses were added.\\n- **The Argument:** Under `scopedBy: 'tenantId'`, public serving callers (browsers or anonymous API clients) lack a tenant scope. `cdn.resolve_site` is the single reviewed bypass into the `site` collection with an explicit invariant: *one site by exact hostname, with nothing to enumerate*. Both CDN and API serving paths share this single narrow door via broker contracts without touching direct database handles.\\n- **Count of Unscoped Reads:** Exactly **1** unscoped read exists across the entire codebase at [`src/cdn/tools/resolve_site.ts:47`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/src/cdn/tools/resolve_site.ts#L47) (`this.siteRepo().find({ query: { host }, limit: 1 })`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### 3. Core Architectural Questions\\n1. **What happens to a request that arrives between a deploy and cache invalidation?**\\n   - The request is served against the previously cached site record and release route table. It never observes a torn or half-migrated state because route table entries are keyed on `${site.id}:${releaseHash}:${site.updatedAt}`. As soon as `cdn.site_deployed` or `site.updated` is received, the host entry is evicted, and the next request builds and caches the new route table.\\n2. **Whether a route can be exposed that the release does not contain?**\\n   - **No.** [`routeTable()`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/src/api/methods/routes.ts#L46-L108) filters all contracts against `release.requires`. Unrequired grants in `site.mesh.contracts` are omitted from the route table and return 404.\\n3. **What a part's declared `requires` means here?**\\n   - Parts declare requirements (`requires: [...]`). Releases aggregate these requirements into `release.requires`. Sites grant permissions and choose gates (`site.mesh.contracts`).\\n   - *A part must never choose its own gate* (otherwise installing an extension would allow privilege escalation). The API server mounts the intersection of what the release requires and what the site grants, at the gate defined by the site operator.\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### 4. Notes for [`spec/unread.md`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/spec/unread.md)\\n- `release.requires` now has active serving-path consumers in [`ApiService.tableFor`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/src/api/api.service.ts#L368-L387) and [`api_describe`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/src/api/tools/describe.ts#L34-L53) to prune unrequired grants at runtime, in addition to compose-time verification in `checkComposition`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### 5. Verification \\u0026 Report\\n- **Unit \\u0026 Integration Tests:**\\n  - Added unit tests in [`test/api/routes.test.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/test/api/routes.test.ts).\\n  - Added integration tests in [`test/integration/api.test.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/test/integration/api.test.ts) covering per-site gates on one node, zero-restart deploy updates, and negative caching of unknown hosts.\\n- **Suite Status:** All 26 test files passed, 315/315 tests passing.\\n- **Typecheck:** `npm run typecheck` exited 0.\\n- **Roadmap \\u0026 Report:**\\n  - [`spec/roadmap.md`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/spec/roadmap.md) updated: **D2** marked complete, M3 milestone line updated.\\n  - Report written to [`agent-runs/reports/6-routes-from-the-record.md`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-serve-dispatch-6/agent-runs/reports/6-routes-from-the-record.md).\\n- **Git Commits on branch `dispatch/6`:**\\n  - `447ea40`: `D2: route resolution derived from site and release records`\\n  - `24842c2`: `test(api): integration tests for per-site gates, dynamic deploys, and unknown hosts`\\n  - `4a2c1ea`: `docs(roadmap): mark D2 complete and update M3 milestone`\\n  - `f784aae`: `docs: report for dispatch 6 (D2 routes from the record)`\\n\",\"duration_seconds\":748.703680233,\"num_turns\":1,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":650892,\"output_tokens\":109211,\"thinking_tokens\":84715,\"cache_read_tokens\":16035570,\"total_tokens\":760103}}}\n./agent-runs/reports/6-routes-from-the-record.md:Furthermore, at composition time, `cdn.compose` runs `checkComposition`, which flags unrequired grants as `unusedGrants` warnings, alerting operators of extraneous exposure.\n./agent-runs/reports/6-routes-from-the-record.md:  - Previously: `release.requires` was computed at compose time and checked by `checkComposition` for unmet dependencies and unused grants, but was unread by the serving path.\n./agent-runs/prompts/8-exposure-hash.prompt.txt:                                     `checkComposition` already refuses a missing\n./agent-runs/prompts/6-routes-from-the-record.prompt.txt:  is the thing `checkComposition` already checks for composition — say whether\n./agent-runs/prompts/2-part-stylesheets.prompt.txt:  shape of problem `checkComposition` already reports.\n./agent-runs/prompts/9-kernel-mismatch.prompt.txt:it. **Nothing reads it.** `checkComposition` checks missing required parts, unmet\n./agent-runs/prompts/9-kernel-mismatch.prompt.txt:    src/cdn/methods/release.ts       checkComposition — the distinctions are the\n./agent-runs/prompts/9-kernel-mismatch.prompt.txt:- whether `checkComposition`'s four problem kinds are still the right set, now\n./spec/roadmap.md:      `checkComposition` alongside it, and the distinctions are the point: a **required** part that is\n./spec/roadmap.md:      has a tool behind it: `compose` resolves against the catalog, runs `check